{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310729,"nonce":"xPEDgtmqEQLUa8ulz1FDHoZk1K0=","title":"tensor.dim(axis) MIR wrapper wired but SIGILLs at runtime despite Tensor_dim being registered — full wiring reverted, root cause ...","message":"UNFIXED, reverted 2026-06-04. Attempted to replace `x.shape()[0]` with `x.dim(0)` in nue (GQAttention/KVCache/MultiHeadAttention) to skip per-call HaxeArray allocation. End-to-end wiring landed:\n\n- `rayzor_tensor_dim(tensor: i64, axis: i64) -\u003e i64` in runtime/src/tensor.rs\n- `register_symbol!(\"rayzor_tensor_dim\", …)` in plugin_impl.rs\n- `build_tensor_dim` MIR wrapper with `InlineHint::Always` in compiler/src/stdlib/tensor.rs\n- `map_method!(instance \"rayzor_ds_Tensor\", \"dim\" =\u003e \"Tensor_dim\", params: 1, mir_wrapper, types: \u0026[PtrVoid, I64] =\u003e I64)` in runtime_mapping.rs\n- `@:native(\"tensor_dim\") public function dim(axis:Int):Int;` in haxe-std Tensor.hx\n\n**Symptom**: EXIT=132 (SIGILL) at first `x.dim(0)` call site, AFTER `[gen] streaming` print. Bisect: ANY single call site → SIGILL; all reverted → works.\n\n**RAYZOR_DUMP_FN_PTRS** confirmed `Tensor_dim` is registered at a valid address (0x10527258c). NO W0020 trap-stub warnings. Symbol exists and resolves.\n\n**Confounds**: Wiring is byte-identical to working `Tensor_get_flat` (params: 1, types: \u0026[PtrVoid, I64]) — only return type differs (F64 vs I64). `numel`/`ndim` work with params: 0 → I64.\n\n**Why:** Profile attribution had this as a P2 optimization (~5% of decode), not load-bearing. Cost of root-causing the dispatch failure exceeded expected win.\n\n**How to apply:** Don't re-attempt `tensor.dim(axis)` extern wiring without first understanding why I64-return MIR wrappers with 1 param dispatch differently from F64-return. Likely candidates to investigate: param ABI marshalling for Haxe `:Int` return type, mir_wrapper return-type lowering for I64 vs F64, or a missing case in the call-site dispatch for instance methods that take 1 non-self arg and return I64 (vs F64 which works, or 0-arg I64 which also works). See [[bugs_array_float_push_any_param.md]] for related (F64,Any) → I64 ABI pitfall — possibly the inverse here.\n\nAlternative path if shape() alloc becomes the dominant cost: HaxeArray pooling, or shape-array caching on `RayzorTensor` so `tensor_shape` returns a stable arr_ptr until reshape.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_tensor_dim_sigill` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}